                    Frequency:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    <strong>TBD</strong> &mdash; will be
                    confirmed in the reminder email; program
                    your radio when announced
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Fox power:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    5+ watts &mdash; wide-area coverage across
                    greater Puget Sound
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Hunt type:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    Mobile T-hunt (drive to bearings) with
                    short on-foot final leg
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </table>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                What to Bring
              </h3>
              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Vehicle</strong> and a co-pilot if
                  possible &mdash; one person drives, one
                  takes bearings
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Mobile or handheld radio on the hunt
                  frequency (TBD)
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Directional antenna &mdash; a Yagi on the
                  vehicle roof mount or a handheld tape-measure
                  Yagi for bearing checks
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Step attenuator for close-in hunting during
                  the final on-foot leg
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Washington state road map or mapping
                  application for triangulating bearings
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Comfortable walking shoes for the final
                  on-foot leg on a forested hillside
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Water, snacks, and a full tank of fuel
                </li>
              </ul>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                About Howarth Park
              </h3>
              <p>
                Howarth Park sits on a bluff above Puget Sound
                at the west end of Everett. The park has picnic
                tables, covered shelters, and great views of the
                water &mdash; an ideal spot for the post-hunt
                social gathering. The forested hillside between
                the upper park and the beach trail will be the
                setting for the final on-foot leg.
              </p>

              <p style="background-color:#fce4e4;border-left:4px solid
                        #c62828;padding:12px 16px;margin:20px 0;
                        font-size:14px;">
                <strong>Safety note:</strong> All foot traffic must
                stay clear of the BNSF railroad tracks and the
                railway bridge near the bottom of the hillside.
                Do not cross the tracks.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                RSVP &amp; Questions
              </h3>
              <p>
                A head count helps us plan the event logistics.
                Reply to this message or contact
                <strong>Tom Sayles, KE4HET</strong> at
                [TOM-EMAIL].
              </p>

              <p>
                More details &mdash; including the start location
                and frequency &mdash; will come in the reminder
                email closer to the event. Watch your inbox!
              </p>

              <p>
                We look forward to seeing you for the season
                finale. 73 de KE4HET
              </p>

